lients.py:610-627 creates a marker but never reads it; the assertions check only the cleanup wording."],"file":"docs/evidence/2026-08-23-cycle13-mutation-proof-portable-copies.txt","finding_id":"F-004","lens_id":"testing","line":31,"owner":"human","pre_existing":false,"requires_verification":true,"severity":"P2","status":"active","suggested_fix":"Either narrow the cycle-13 claim to the caveat the test actually proves, or make the test observe and clean up the escaped descendant deterministically; regenerate the bound proof rather than editing its digest by hand.","title":"Mutation proof overstates escaped-session coverage","touched_paths":["docs/evidence/2026-08-23-cycle13-mutation-proof-portable-copies.txt","tests/test_assess_clients.py"],"why_it_matters":"The committed proof tells reviewers that escaped-descendant survival was observed, but the test explicitly does not assert that, so the evidence overstates what zero survivors establishes."},{"autofix_class":"gated_auto","confidence":100,"dimension_id":"serialization-errors","evidence":["scripts/assess_clients.py:1147-1154 writes -1 for a deadline and calls it a status no real exit can produce.","A real subprocess terminated by SIGHUP and a later timed-out subprocess both serialized as exit_status -1 in the same blocked stage.","schemas/compatibility-matrix.schema.json:222-224 accepts every integer and carries no timed-out state; the validator also accepted -1 with an arbitrary blocked reason."],"file":"scripts/assess_clients.py","finding_id":"F-005","lens_id":"api-contract","line":1150,"owner":"review-fixer","pre_existing":false,"requires_verification":true,"severity":"P2","status":"active","suggested_fix":"Give version two an explicit per-command termination state, or a nullable exit status with enforced semantics, then update the producer, schema, validator, runbook, and behavior tests together so a real negative signal return remains distinct.","title":"Timeout sentinel collides with real signal status","touched_paths":["scripts/assess_clients.py","schemas/compatibility-matrix.schema.json","scripts/check_compatibility_matrix.py","tests/test_assess_clients.py","tests/test_check_compatibility_matrix.py","docs/runbooks/portable-plugin-port.md"],"why_it_matters":"A version-two consumer cannot tell which command with status -1 was killed at its deadline and which completed after signal 1, so the per-command status record is not machine-actionable."},{"autofix_class":"gated_auto","confidence":100,"dimension_id":"state-data-invariants-transactions-concurrency","evidence":["scripts/assess_clients.py:1414 trusts any truthy supplied run_directory without checking that it is new, empty, or belongs to workspace.","A direct probe supplied a directory holding openai-codex/package, assessed Claude Code successfully, and left both package copies in the same run directory.","scripts/assess_clients.py:1609 writes transcript.json under the supplied directory with the overwrite-capable write_private path."],"file":"scripts/assess_clients.py","finding_id":"F-006","lens_id":"correctness","line":1414,"owner":"review-fixer","pre_existing":false,"requires_verification":true,"severity":"P2","status":"active","suggested_fix":"Validate a supplied run_directory as an existing empty directory allocated for this call, reject a mismatch with workspace, and add a regression with a stale package copy and transcript while keeping the no-argument fallback allocation unchanged.","title":"Supplied run directories bypass freshness","touched_paths":["scripts/assess_clients.py","tests/test_assess_clients.py"],"why_it_matters":"A direct caller can mix a new assessment into a prior run directory and overwrite that run's transcript, defeating the one-run-one-directory evidence boundary."},{"autofix_class":"gated_auto","confidence":100,"dimension_id":"interface-contract-compatibility","evidence":["schemas/compatibility-matrix.schema.json:206-224 says command remains the first commands entry for version two.","scripts/check_compatibility_matrix.py:749-750 skips every non-executed stage before the alias agreement check at lines 757-762.","A validator probe with a blocked stage, command='first-command', commands[0].command='different-command', and exit_status=-1 returned no problems."],"file":"scripts/check_compatibility_matrix.py","finding_id":"F-007","lens_id":"api-contract","line":749,"owner":"review-fixer","pre_existing":false,"requires_verification":true,"severity":"P2","status":"active","suggested_fix":"Enforce command equals commands[0].command whenever a non-empty version-two commands list is present, including blocked stages, and add a blocked-row disagreement regression.","title":"Blocked command aliases escape validation","touched_paths":["scripts/check_compatibility_matrix.py","tests/test_check_compatibility_matrix.py"],"why_it_matters":"A version-two blocked row can name one command in command and a different first command in commands while the validator reports success, so readers and safety consumers receive contradictory evidence."}],"fix_requests":[{"autofix_class":"gated_auto","finding_ids":["F-005","F-006","F-007"],"fix_id":"FIX-002","owner":"review-fixer","requires_verification":true,"summary":"Repair the version-two timeout and blocked-alias contracts while preserving the fresh run-directory invariant.","touched_paths":["docs/runbooks/portable-plugin-port.md","schemas/compatibility-matrix.schema.json","scripts/assess_clients.py","scripts/check_compatibility_matrix.py","tests/test_assess_clients.py","tests/test_check_compatibility_matrix.py"]},{"autofix_class":"manual","finding_ids":["F-004"],"fix_id":"FIX-003","owner":"human","requires_verification":true,"summary":"Align the cycle-13 escaped-session claim with the behavior its test actually proves.","touched_paths":["docs/evidence/2026-08-23-cycle13-mutation-proof-portable-copies.txt","tests/test_assess_clients.py"]}],"lens_results":[{"accepted":false,"applicable_dimensions":{"resolution-completeness":7.0},